# Copy to server/.env. Provider calls are made in-process (adr-007) — set a
# key per provider you want routable; models whose provider has no key fail
# instantly and the routing walk moves on.

# Free-tier MVP keys (the default routes in routing.ts run on these):
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# Optional paid fallbacks / BYOK providers:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Local Ollama (dev-only gemma3-4b fallback); default shown:
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Operator-cost guardrails (adr-008); defaults shown, 0 disables one.
# BYOK requests are exempt — they spend the caller's key.
# LIMIT_GENERATIONS_PER_DAY=10
# LIMIT_REGENERATIONS_PER_DAY=30
# LIMIT_BACKGROUNDS_PER_DAY=3
# DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5

# Custom domain (docs/05-deployment.md): redirect every other host (e.g. the
# platform *.code.run endpoint) to this one. Unset = no redirect.
# CANONICAL_HOST=invito.example.com

# Host sign-in with Google (adr-014). Both unset = sign-in is off and publish
# stays anonymous, which is a supported mode — local development and
# self-hosting need no OAuth client. Create credentials at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (OAuth client, type "Web
# application") and register the callback below as an authorized redirect URI.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=....apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#
# The callback URI is derived from the incoming request, so
# http://localhost:3001/api/auth/google/callback works in development with
# nothing set here. Set it explicitly in production: Google matches it against
# its registered allowlist, and a deployment behind CANONICAL_HOST must send
# the canonical host rather than the platform one.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://invito.example.com/api/auth/google/callback

# PORT=3001
